  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only multiprofile with scvi_n200 is the strongest configuration (0.653 acc / 0.628 F1, config_006), and image-only models are very weak (best: ViT-L at 0.227 acc, config_013). The single biggest design lever identified is multiprofile (+13 pts over single-profile), and scvi_n200 is the best RNA encoder. The critical remaining uncertainty is whether fusing the weak image signal with the strong RNA signal adds any value. This experiment (config_039) pairs the best RNA encoder (scvi_n200), best image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), multiprofile, transformer aggregation, and weighted fusion—directly testing whether weighted multimodal fusion can improve on the 0.653 RNA-only baseline. Weighted fusion is chosen over concat because it can learn to downweight a weak modality, making it the most informative test: if even weighted fusion fails to beat the RNA-only result, it provides strong evidence that image contributes little and further multimodal exploration is not worthwhile under a limited budget. This single experiment resolves the highest-impact open design question before committing additional budget to the 20+ remaining multimodal configurations."
}

